Your quiet, solitary life as a gardener in the apocalypse remains undisturbed.
Eventually, all the batteries die. Time blurs, so you start keeping a diary.
Days pass. Sometimes you wonder if you’re the last person alive on Earth. Sometimes you wish this was all staged, similar to the Truman Show.
Would the crew feel sorry for you? Maybe tomorrow, as soon as tomorrow, they’ll finally knock on your door with confetti, cakes and martinis to celebrate the wrap. The wrap!!
The wrap…When will it come? How much longer can this last?
How much longer can you wait?
It could be one more day. It could be eternity.